/// The blocks of the report that are counted: inverter, nand, nor, tgate, dff, dynamic_comparator, tracking_switch, clock_gen, SAR_logic, DAC_control, DAC_control_top,
/// neg_bottom_plate_logic, and the 11-bit integration run. The corners smoke suite is a test run over five corners and three temperatures, not a block: it is a line of its own.
pub const AS_N_BLOCKS : u32 = 13;
/// The rows of those blocks: 30 (inverter 2, nand 2, nor 2, tgate 3, dff 3, dynamic_comparator 4, tracking_switch 3, clock_gen 4, SAR_logic 2, DAC_control 1, DAC_control_top 1, neg_bottom_plate_logic 1, integration 2).
pub const AS_N_ROWS : u32 = 30;

; --- why a row is NOT MODELLED (one reason per kind, quoted by the doc) ---------------------------------------------
pub const AS_WHY_INV_DELAY : str = "the transient is validated at 500 fF and 10 pF only; at 20 fF the gate edge kicks the output outside the tables' 0 to Vdd range";
pub const AS_WHY_LEVELS : str = "the model is gate level: a node is 0, 1 or X, never a voltage";
pub const AS_WHY_TG_RON : str = "a read with no body effect (Vsb forced to 0) puts ours 30 percent under ngspice's real cell at 0.75 V and 24 percent under at the worst point, past the 10 percent bar; with each bulk tied to its source ngspice agrees with ours to 0.06 percent; with the source-to-bulk axis (M3e) the rows are measured and PASS";
pub const AS_WHY_SW_HOLD : str = "square law: no gate capacitance, so no charge injection; the hold step the model returns is a following artifact of 0.18 uV";
pub const AS_WHY_SW_DROOP : str = "square law: no leakage; the droop the model returns is exactly zero by construction";
pub const AS_WHY_DAC_CONTROL : str = "the DAC takes its plate levels as ideal sources: the level is the input, not a result";
pub const AS_WHY_DAC_TOP : str = "the eleven latches and the plate lines are not a circuit in any spec; the converter's decision order is behavioural";
pub const AS_WHY_NEG_PLATE : str = "the N half's follow-then-complement logic is not a circuit in any spec; the DAC model has the N plate move reversed by construction";
pub const AS_WHY_CORNERS : str = "the tables have five corners at 27 C (tt also at 50 C) and none at -40 or 125 C; the report's suite is five corners at three temperatures";

